My rice for DWM - Dynamic Window Manager by Suckless.org
============================
dwm is an extremely fast, small, and dynamic window manager for X.


Requirements
------------
In order to build dwm you need the Xlib header files.


Installation
------------
Edit config.mk to match your local setup (dwm is installed into
the /usr/local namespace by default).

Afterwards enter the following command to build and install dwm (if
necessary as root):

    make clean install


Running dwm
-----------
Add the following line to your .xinitrc to start dwm using startx:

    exec dwm

In order to connect dwm to a specific display, make sure that
the DISPLAY environment variable is set correctly, e.g.:

    DISPLAY=foo.bar:1 exec dwm

(This will start dwm on display :1 of the host foo.bar.)

In order to display status info in the bar, you can do something
like this in your .xinitrc:

    while xsetroot -name "`date` `uptime | sed 's/.*,//'`"
    do
    	sleep 1
    done &
    exec dwm


Configuration
-------------
The configuration of dwm is done by creating a custom config.h
and (re)compiling the source code.


Control keybinds
-------------

Modkey - Alt

Launching
Alt + p                      - open rofi (dmenu is also configured, change as you like)
Alt + Shift + Enter          - spawn terminal (st)
Alt + Shift + c              - close focused window
Alt + Shift + q              - quit dwm

Windows
Alt + j/k                    - focus next/previous window
Alt + Enter                  - swap focused window with master
Alt + i/d                    - add/remove a window in the master area
Alt + h/l                    - shrink/grow the master area
Alt + Shift + Space          - toggle focused window floating/tiled
Alt + b                      - show/hide bar

Layouts
Alt + t                      - tile (default)
Alt + f                      - floating
Alt + m                      - monocle (one window at a time, fullscreen)
Alt + u                      - centered master, others tiled around it
Alt + o                      - centered floating master
Alt + Space                  - toggle between current and previous layout

Tags
Alt + 1-9                    - view tag
Alt + Tab                    - switch between current and previous tag
Alt + Shift + 1-9            - move focused window to tag
Alt + Control + 1-9          - add/remove tag from current view (view multiple tags)
Alt + Shift + Control + 1-9  - add/remove tag on focused window (show it on several tags)
Alt + 0                      - view all tags at once
Alt + Shift + 0              - show focused window on all tags

Monitors
Alt + , / .                  - focus previous/next monitor
Alt + Shift + , / .          - move focused window to previous/next monitor
Super + 0/1/2                - focus monitor 1/2/3
Super + Shift + 0/1/2        - move focused window to monitor 1/2/3

Gaps
Alt + -  / Alt + =           - decrease / increase gaps
Alt + Shift + =              - reset gaps to default

Media keys
Volume up/down/mute, brightness up/down (no modifier)
